<DocsLayout
  slug="analytics"
  title="Analytics"
  description="Success rate, duration, and trends for every project."
>
  <h2 id="whats-tracked">What's tracked</h2>
  <p>
    Every finished build — success, failed, or cancelled — is recorded: total builds, success
    rate, and average duration, broken down by platform (Android/iOS) and environment
    (staging/production).
  </p>

  <h2 id="where-to-find-it">Where to find it</h2>
  <p>
    A project's Analytics tab shows the current month's summary, plus a trend chart covering the
    last 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-it-stays-accurate">How it stays accurate</h2>
  <p>
    pkgr.app listens for GitHub's own build-completed webhook, in addition to polling from the
    dashboard, so a build is recorded whether or not anyone has the app open when it finishes. One
    caveat: builds that finished before this webhook went live weren't backfilled, so very old
    projects may show a gap for that early period.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
